{"title":"1987 IMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Problems of the 1987 IMO Cuba.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_I\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day I</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Resources\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Resources</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_I\">Day I</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day I\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/9/0c9de4a5aca7038f6109d3229f75279ec06134b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_n (k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" /> be the number of permutations of the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/0/470896f803f9cb53cc8cbc85e9412d5277058255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{ 1, \\ldots , n \\} , \\; n \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"18\" />, which have exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> fixed points.  Prove that\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/4/c24794c6daa6d075482766c4391249478ed0e8f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=0}^{n} k \\cdot p_n (k) = n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"133\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>(Remark: A permutation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> of a set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is a one-to-one mapping of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> onto itself.  An element <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is called a fixed point of the permutation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/e/ffee37bffac821b0cf5d9da5fc0127064aed9db0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(i) = i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />.)\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1987 IMO Problems/Problem 1\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>In an acute-angled triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> the interior bisector of the angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> and intersects the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circumcircle\" title=\"Circumcircle\">circumcircle</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> again at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. From point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> perpendiculars are drawn to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, the feet of these perpendiculars being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> respectively.  Prove that the quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/9/709bc1bfd9a47f70af3aadfe3e01039fc04f8d90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AKNM$\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" /> and the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> have equal areas. \n</p><p><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1987 IMO Problems/Problem 2\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/2/a92b05d5612fcc21302bf43d1a9b4328272dead8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 , x_2 , \\ldots , x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"13\" /> be real numbers satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/b/99bdaf7026430c298205076d1bd290f47bca56e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1^2 + x_2^2 + \\cdots + x_n^2 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"175\" height=\"19\" />.  Prove that for every integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c17d88e2fdeef66df0e37def936f39b773567278.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> there are integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/5/bd564b1c10a67cf00881302683c362ee6e5ce2a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, \\ldots a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"92\" height=\"11\" />, not all 0, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/f/9bfc93dee4ad0d4203fd93f5bd9121099be4be52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$| a_i | \\le k-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> and\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/b/e0bb539dbf6b18b2ad571def18ee760a31125282.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a_1x_1 + a_2x_2 + \\cdots + a_nx_n| \\le \\frac{ (k-1) \\sqrt{n} }{ k^n - 1 }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"314\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1987 IMO Problems/Problem 3\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Prove that there is no function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> from the set of non-negative  integers into itself such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/0/8b00deabc03d13dd856d0d6087ec282becaada30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(f(n)) = n + 1987$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"154\" height=\"18\" /> for every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1987 IMO Problems/Problem 4\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be an integer greater than or equal to 3.  Prove that there is a set of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> points in the plane such that the distance between any two points is irrational and each set of three points determines a non-degenerate triangle with rational area.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1987 IMO Problems/Problem 5\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be an integer greater than or equal to 2.  Prove that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/7/8270364deeb06f16f99d36b56ed64d8f8a4c1dfd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2 + k + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"16\" /> is prime for all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/1/cf17b6450d5166508952da39ad1d172ae83e80ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq k \\leq \\sqrt{n/3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"115\" height=\"32\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/7/8270364deeb06f16f99d36b56ed64d8f8a4c1dfd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2 + k + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"16\" /> is prime for all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/3/953e6460a4443c708f22cbc366bc43a5ac4900f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq k \\leq n - 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"109\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1987 IMO Problems/Problem 6\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_IMO\" title=\"1987 IMO\">1987 IMO</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=1&amp;cid=16&amp;year=1987\">IMO 1987 problems on the Resources page</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\">IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competition resources\">Mathematics competition resources</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_IMO\" title=\"1987 IMO\">1987 IMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_IMO\" title=\"1986 IMO\">1986 IMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1987 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1987 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1987 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1987 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1987 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1987 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_IMO\" title=\"1988 IMO\">1988 IMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018043229\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.030 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.046 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 270/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 837/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 56/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7670/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.423      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.423      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4330:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018043229 and revision id 198312. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}